:"2015-10-19T09:05:53Z","body":"The entry in `WORKSPACE`:\n\n```\nnew_http_archive(\n  name = \"boost\",\n  url = \"http://boost.org/archive.zip\",\n  build_file = \"my.BUILD\",\n)\n```\n\nand a `my.BUILD` with\n\n```\ncc_library(\n  name = \"my\",\n  srcs = \"@boost//glorioussource.cpp\",\n)\n```\n\nshould demonstrate the issue.\nThere may be one reason, when this may make sense - when you use `my.BUILD/my` from different repos.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/149152322/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"abergmeier","id":2580183,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1ODAxODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2580183?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/abergmeier","html_url":"https://github.com/abergmeier","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abergmeier/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abergmeier/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abergmeier/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abergmeier/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abergmeier/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abergmeier/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abergmeier/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abergmeier/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/abergmeier/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/149160887","html_url":"https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/517#issuecomment-149160887","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/517","id":149160887,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0OTE2MDg4Nw==","user":{"login":"lberki","id":3524818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MjQ4MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3524818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki","html_url":"https://github.com/lberki","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lberki/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2015-10-19T09:33:27Z","updated_at":"2015-10-19T09:33:54Z","body":"Can't reproduce (if for no other reason, but because `http://boost.org/archive.zip` is a 404... it also seems strange, because in a repository called `boost`, `@boost//:foo` is exactly equivalent to `//:foo`. What error message do you get? Maybe you need to add the `includes=[\".\"]` attribute to your cc_library?\n\nI tried this and it worked alright:\n\n```\necho 'new_local_repository(name=\"l\", path=__workspace_dir__ + \"/l\", build_file=\"my.BUILD\")' > WORKSPACE\ncat > my.BUILD <<EOF\ncc_library(name = \"c\", hdrs = [\"c.h\"])\ncc_binary(name=\"cb\", deps=[\"@l//:c\"], srcs=[\"cb.cc\"])\nEOF\nmkdir l\necho '#define MACRO 42' > l/c.h\ncat > l/cb.cc <<EOF\n#include \"c.h\"\nint main(void) { return MACRO; }\nEOF\nbazel build @l//:cb\n```\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/comments/149160887/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"